%% posix-on-wasm.mgp - POSIX on WebAssembly (or: what is an OS anyway?)
%% A gucOS talk (todos/0221). Slides are cue cards - the speaker carries
%% the argument. Uses only directives the 0119 port renders (the 0202
%% whitelist).
%deffont "standard" tfont "/usr/share/fonts/mono.ttf"
%default 1 area 90 90, size 2, fore "white", back "#301848", font "standard"
%default 2 size 8, vgap 20, prefix " ", center
%default 3 size 5, fore "yellow", vgap 30
%tab 1 size 4, vgap 40, prefix "  ", icon box "SpringGreen" 50, left
%tab 2 size 3, vgap 40, prefix "      ", icon arc "gold" 50, left
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

POSIX on WebAssembly

or: what is an OS anyway?

%center
%size 3, fore "gray70"
space / click: next    b: back    q: quit
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

What is an OS anyway?

	"it talks to the hardware for you"
	true. one job of many.
	an OS multiplexes the machine:
		CPU - scheduler
		screen - compositor
		audio - mixer
		disk - filesystem
		input - focus
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

What is POSIX?

	the Unix contract. IEEE 1003, 1988.
	files, processes, signals, pipes, terminals
	an API and its semantics
	not a kernel. not a desktop.
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

Isn't emscripten POSIX?

	yes: one Unix program, compiled for the browser
	no: one program is not a system
		no processes, no shell, no desktop
	building that is the actual work
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

gucOS

	an operating system in a browser tab
	every binary is a wasm module
	built by its own compiler, inside it
	the OS job list, three ways:
%size 6, center, fore "SpringGreen"
DO
%size 6, center, fore "orange"
DON'T
%size 6, center, fore "DeepSkyBlue"
DON'T NEED TO
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

DO: processes

	one worker per process. own memory.
	pids, pipes, ptys, wait, kill, job control
	spawn, not fork
	pid 1 is busybox hush
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

DO: a shared world

	BlockFS - files survive the tab
	a compositor and a window manager
	a sound server - N processes, one output
	cc hello.c inside the OS. it runs.
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

DON'T: threads

	no pthreads. no atomics for programs.
	processes are the unit of parallelism
	the kernel underneath is built on both
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

DON'T: fork

	fork clones a live process. wasm can't.
	gucOS: posix_spawn
		WSL1 built real fork on NT - its slowest part
		Microsoft's fix was WSL2: a whole VM
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

DON'T: preemption

	signals land at safe points
	a busy loop cannot be interrupted
	SIGKILL still works - the worker dies
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

DON'T NEED TO: schedule

	gucOS has no scheduler
	each process is a real OS thread
	the machine preempts them. all cores.
	lost: priorities, nice, CPU accounting
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

DON'T NEED TO: the rest

	drivers - the browser has them
	MMU - wasm cannot make a bad address
	boot - the tab is the boot
	ext4 - there is no disk
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

The browser is the HAL

%size 3, fore "gray70", center
hardware abstraction layer
%size 5, fore "white", left, prefix 20

display     WebGPU
audio       Web Audio
storage     OPFS
input       browser events
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

How slow is it?

	a syscall is a message to the kernel worker
	~10us. Linux: ~0.5us.
	so hot paths leave the kernel:
		getpid - a vDSO page, no syscall
		/usr reads - local, 496 -> 1345 MB/s
		pipes - shared rings, 272 -> 443 MB/s
		an 8MB pipe job: 280 syscalls down to 4
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

Why not emulate?

	tinyemu and v86 emulate a whole CPU
	they can preempt at any instruction
	they pay at every instruction
	gucOS pays only at syscalls
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

Prior art

	Browsix - same idea. has fork. no desktop.
	WASIX - full POSIX on wasm. pays for it.
	tinyemu / v86 - emulators. boot real Linux.
	WebVM / CheerpX - x86 JIT in a tab
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

The end

	this deck is a text file on the OS it describes
	right-click it, pick Edit
	ctrl-r reloads
